LEGACY RETAIL ETL MODERNIZATION
**********************************************************************************************************************************************************             
OVERVIEW
________

•	I worked on migrating legacy SSIS-based retail ETL pipelines to Azure cloud architecture.
•	Initially, we analyzed existing SSIS packages, dependencies, source systems, and data volumes, which were around 20 million daily retail transactions.
•	We designed a Medallion architecture using ADLS Bronze, Silver, and Gold layers.
•	ADF pipelines were developed for incremental ingestion from SQL Server, APIs, and CSV files into Bronze storage.
•	PySpark transformations in Databricks handled cleansing, deduplication, joins, standardization, and KPI calculations on large-scale datasets.
•	We optimized Spark jobs using partitioning, broadcast joins, and Delta Lake optimizations, improving throughput by 3x.
•	Gold layer business metrics were consumed in Power BI dashboards for sales, inventory, and customer analytics.
•	We implemented CI/CD using Azure DevOps and enabled blue-green deployments for zero-downtime releases while

